  "notes": [
    "Two metrics moved far beyond tolerance and both are consequences of construction working. referenceLivingMages 105.5 -> 189.8 (4.31 SE) and referenceLibraryDepth 9.94 -> 29.17 (5.91 SE): universities founded by the god now get finished by laborers, so they open seats, seats take students, students become mages, and mages fill libraries. mc-harness recorded the old behaviour as 'universities-are-founded-and-never-finished' and that entry is annotated on this branch rather than deleted. referencePeakPopulation 50080 -> 29489 (-156 SE) is the other side of the same change and is the number most worth an author's attention: carrying capacity's provisioning multiplier now reads the food stock alone rather than every material summed, and laborers standing on a building site produce nothing that month. Both are documented decisions, neither is tuned, and if the intended world is one where a god may not halve its own peak population by over-founding then the lever is a cap on the divertible labour share, which this branch deliberately did not invent. perRunTimeoutMs was also raised from 600000 to 1800000: one archivist run now takes 305 s alone, measured, against a cap sized for a build whose universities never completed. pool.ts says the budget is sized against what the simulation does, and the simulation now does more."
  ],
